The paper’s strongest contribution (a decoupled scene×environment adapter) is tightly coupled to a **retrieval-based implicit task identifier** (§3.4). This coupling means the work is best interpreted not as “task-id free continual VLN” in the usual sense, but as “continual VLN with test-time expert retrieval”; making that framing explicit—and quantifying routing robustness—would substantially clarify what is being solved and why the reported improvements hold.

