Calibration could not be performed because `calibration_search` consistently failed with a tool error (“not a valid model ID”), so I cannot anchor against the human-review corpus as requested. Based on the paper itself: the core technical idea and linearized-regime results look strong, but two headline claims (“dataless” and O(1) merging) are currently over-claimed / under-justified relative to the evidence, which I weigh as major but fixable via claim-tightening plus additional analysis.

